      "content": "To establish a distinct \"raw\" identity without simply pathologizing them, imagine the Low-Tier features are characterized by oversized, active sensory bone structures—like protruding brow ridges or expanded shoulder ribs—that reflect a historical reliance on physical labor and survival instincts rather than refined aesthetics. Their language would likely prioritize immediate, rhythmic intonation with exaggerated head movements to convey emotion, standing in stark contrast to the Elites' precise, delayed, and glass-smooth delivery. Additionally, their body posture should appear coiled and ready to spring, utilizing micro-movements born of constant vigilance, whereas the Elites move with rigid, floating buoyancy that suggests they also move in low-gravity environments. This creates a visual narrative where the Low-Tier feel like untamed, hyper-aware humans, rejecting the sanitized stillness of the Elites.",
